    "knowledge_point": "Comparing an Exponential Function and a Logarithmic Function",
    "problem": "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6x)}.$",
    "worked_solution": "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{2x}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6x)$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(6x)}=\\infty .\n$$",
